# MySQL 8 exact-value arithmetic. A number with a decimal point and no exponent is an exact
# DECIMAL; `/` gives DECIMAL with the dividend's scale plus div_precision_increment (4) and
# rounds once, at the end of an arithmetic expression; `*` adds the scales; DIV is integer
# division; MOD and % keep the dividend's sign. Expected values come from MySQL 8.0.40.

